      "question": "BDS",
      "answer": "Okay! For BDS (Bachelor of Dental Surgery) admissions, you'll find the relevant information on the KGMU website. Here's what you should know:\n\n**Admission Process:**\n\n*   Admissions are based on the NEET (National Eligibility cum Entrance Test) score.\n*   You'll need to participate in the counseling process conducted by the relevant authorities (likely the state or central counseling).\n*   Keep an eye on the official KGMU website and the counseling website for announcements regarding the admission process, registration, merit lists, and counseling dates.\n\n**Key Resources:**\n\n*   **KGMU Website:** [www.kgmu.org](http://www.kgmu.org/) (Check the \"Courses/Admission\" section)\n*   **Dental Course Information:** You can find details specific to the BDS program, including eligibility criteria, the number of seats, and other important information.\n*   **Examination Result:** While not directly related to admission, you may need to check the NEET results on the official website.\n*   **Important Notices:** Keep an eye on the \"Notice Board\" section of the KGMU website for any updates or announcements related to BDS admissions.\n\nTo get started, I recommend visiting the KGMU website and looking for the \"Courses/Admission\" or \"Admissions\" section. There, you should find detailed information about the BDS program, eligibility requirements, and the admission process.\n",
